  "coding_notes": [
    "GAP-CANDIDATE set_notation — q22(a)(i),(a)(ii),(b),(c): FOUR parts, 5 marks, ALL UNTAGGED. This is the strongest evidence in the corpus and it breaks the three-untagged-items allowance on purpose. The question gives a universal set and three sets by rule, then asks for the members of a union, the members of a complement-intersection, whether an intersection equals the empty set with a reason, and the members of a fourth set defined by an empty intersection. There is NO VENN DIAGRAM and no probability anywhere in it. venn_diagrams was rejected as an interim tag here: its topic is Probability and Data, its prerequisites are mutually_exclusive_events and combined_events, and its own example is a counting-from-a-Venn question — tagging it would credit four probability skills for a question containing none. Nothing else in data/skills.ts covers set operations, so untagged beats mis-tagged. topic set to number, matching spec 1.5's placement under Numbers and the number system. This takes set_notation to SEVEN parts on the Foundation slice, well past minParts=4.",
    "NOTE ON THE UNTAGGED COUNT: this paper has 4 untagged items against the registry's allowance of 3, so it cannot be registered until set_notation exists or the rows are retagged. That is the intended consequence rather than a coding slip — the allowance exists to catch sloppy tagging, and here it is correctly reporting a taxonomy gap big enough to need closing.",
    "CORRECTION made while coding: q22(c) was first read from the extracted text as a SUBSET condition, which would have put it in the Higher half of the set split. The mark scheme shows it is D intersect (A union C) = empty set, with answer 23, 25, 29, 31. No subset notation appears. The Foundation/Higher split in docs/audit/25-igcse-4ma1-delta.md section 2.2 (membership vs cardinality) is unaffected — there is still no n() on any coded Foundation paper.",
    "mark_split values are read off the mark scheme's code sequence where the extraction is unambiguous, and otherwise follow the standard Edexcel shape for that mark count (B1 for a one-mark recall, M1 A1 for two, M1 M1 A1 for three, and so on). q22's are verified directly against the mark scheme.",
    "q5(a)(ii) tagged lowest_common_multiple: 'a multiple of both 4 and 6' is the LCM idea even though the word is not used.",
    "q4(c) tagged time_calculations for reading an analogue clock face, and q4(d) converting_measurements for choosing a sensible metric unit."
  ],
